# sdkconfig overlay applied ONLY to -DTR_BS_BOARD=3 builds, on top of
# sdkconfig.defaults. Selected by the project CMakeLists, not by the build-dir
# name — see there.
#
# Exists because the boot NOR size is a board fact and sdkconfig is
# per-project. V1/V2 fit a W25Q64 (8 MB); V3 — the PCB V5/V6 hardware, fabbed
# after the 2026-08-09 close-out — fits a GD25Q128ESIG (16 MB). Declaring 16 MB
# against a V2's 8 MB part is a boot loop inside the bootloader, before any
# firmware runs, so the base file declares the small value and this file raises
# it for the one board that has the part.

# === Boot NOR: 16 MB, and the partition table that needs it ===
# These two lines are a pair. Unlike flight_computer and out_computer, where
# the flash size is purely a declaration and every board shares one table, the
# BS layouts genuinely differ: V3 has NO external NAND (board_v3.h,
# HAS_EXT_NAND = false), so spiffs is its only log store and #835 item 1 grew
# it to 9.94 MB — a table that does not fit in 8 MB at all.
#
# Splitting them would not merely be untidy, it would not build:
# gen_esp32part.py rejects a table larger than the declared flash size
#   "Partitions tables occupies 16.0MB of flash ... which does not fit in
#    configured flash size 8MB"
# which is exactly the check that should fire, and does, if these drift apart.
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE_16MB=y
CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM_FILENAME="partitions_v3.csv"
